    description:
      "We're including the Sunny SF-T7515 as our reference point for manual latch folding, the most common mechanism on the market and the one most first-time buyers will actually encounter. Its 2.2 CHP motor and 39-inch deck are tuned for walking and light jogging rather than sprint work, which fits its role as an entry-level pick. Folded, it measures around 32 x 28 inches and weighs roughly 62 pounds, genuinely a one-person lift onto its transport wheels. We folded and unfolded it daily for ten days specifically to evaluate the latch mechanism on its own terms, and it held up consistently, though it does require a firmer, deliberate push to seat fully compared to the assisted hinges on pricier machines — a good demonstration of why manual latches ask more of the user physically even when they're mechanically sound. The console is intentionally simple: speed, time, distance, calories, with no touchscreen and no app requirement, which several testers actually preferred for its lack of friction. Weight capacity tops out at 220 pounds, lower than mid-range folding machines, so it's worth checking that figure against your household. At a typical price under <strong>$300</strong>, it's the most affordable machine in this guide, and it proves that a well-built manual latch doesn't need to feel flimsy, it just needs a bit more intentional effort from the person operating it.",
  },
  {
    id: "nordictrack-t65s",
    name: "NordicTrack T Series 6.5 S",
    category: "Folding Interactive Treadmill",
    badge: "EasyLift Assist Example",
    amazonUrl:
      "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=NordicTrack+T+Series+6.5+S+Treadmill&tag=sktiger-20",
    rating: 4.4,
    reviewCount: 2894,
    pros: [
      "EasyLift assist sits between manual and full hydraulic in effort required",
