      "We included the Horizon T101 specifically to highlight a design detail that matters more than most spec sheets emphasize: a secondary safety pin layered on top of the primary fold latch. Across six weeks of rotating multiple household members through this machine, the two-stage lock never once let the deck drop unexpectedly, even when testers deliberately tried to release the latch without fully disengaging the pin first, which is exactly the failure mode a secondary lock exists to prevent. Beyond the mechanism itself, the T101 is a genuinely well-rounded machine: Elite Cushioning softens impact at the front of the deck where your heel strikes and firms up toward the back where you push off, and testers with knee sensitivity specifically called it out as easier on their joints. The deck is a comfortable 20 x 55 inches with a 2.5 CHP motor and 300-pound weight capacity, and folded dimensions come in around 34 x 66 inches, a bit larger than the ultra-compact machines but still manageable against a wall. Bluetooth speakers and compatibility with the Horizon workout app round out the package. Typical pricing lands around <strong>$700-$900</strong>. If you're shopping specifically with a toddler or a curious dog in the house, look for this exact feature, a secondary pin lock in addition to the primary latch, before anything else on the spec sheet.",
